":"daniel@makrotopia.org"},{"name":"David S. Miller","address":"davem@davemloft.net"},{"name":"David Wu","address":"david.wu@rock-chips.com"},{"name":"Eric Dumazet","address":"edumazet@google.com"},{"name":"Greg Kroah-Hartman","address":"gregkh@linuxfoundation.org"},{"name":"Heiko Stuebner","address":"heiko@sntech.de"},{"name":"Herbert Xu","address":"herbert@gondor.apana.org.au"},{"name":"Krzysztof Kozlowski","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Mark Brown","address":"broonie@kernel.org"},{"name":"Maxime Chevallier","address":"maxime.chevallier@bootlin.com"},{"name":"Maxime Coquelin","address":"mcoquelin.stm32@gmail.com"},{"name":"Michael Turquette","address":"mturquette@baylibre.com"},{"name":"Neil Armstrong","address":"neil.armstrong@linaro.org"},{"name":"Nicolas Frattaroli","address":"nicolas.frattaroli@collabora.com"},{"name":"Olivia Mackall","address":"olivia@selenic.com"},{"name":"Paolo Abeni","address":"pabeni@redhat.com"},{"name":"Philipp Zabel","address":"p.zabel@pengutronix.de"},{"name":"Rob Herring","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Stephen Boyd","address":"sboyd@kernel.org"},{"name":"Vinod Koul","address":"vkoul@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-crypto@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-phy@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pwm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-spi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-stm32@st-md-mailman.stormreply.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-usb@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"netdev@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T10:18:45.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T10:18:45.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 00/25] ARM: rockchip: Add peripheral support for RV1106","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Tue, Aug 11, 2026 at 07:43:16AM +0200, Uwe Kleine-König wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"On Mon, Aug 10, 2026 at 11:35:48AM -0700, Jakub Kicinski wrote:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> On Mon, 10 Aug 2026 15:10:51 +0300 Vladislav Leonov wrote:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Basic support for the Rockchip RV1106/RV1103 SoCs currently under review."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > This series builds on top of that and enables the peripherals needed to"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > bring up a board beyond a serial console:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> Don't expect maintainers to dig out patches for their subsystems"},{"depth":1,"text":"> from a big series. This is not how upstream development works."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I see this from time to time and I personally think it's fine to have"},{"depth":1,"text":"these patches together. Also the only the patch that affects my"},{"depth":1,"text":"subsystem was Cc:d to me which is how I like it (but I think opinions"},{"depth":1,"text":"differ on that one, too)."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"`b4 am -P _` is great!"}],"lineCount":15,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Yeah, and with DTS being patch 3, patch 6, 10 ...  and so on, it is\nevery easy to review and pick up."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"No, there is only one case of combining multiple subsystems together -\nupstreaming new SoC vendor. All other cases are wrong and spreading DTS\nall over is just proof that this is poorly readable and poorly\nreviewable."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Not even mentioning the rules of dependency on DTS expressed in\nsubmitting patches."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Best regards,\nKrzysztof"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"anq1ouUnKA02Eauj@monoceros"},"20260814-resilient-handsome-ibis-d5efdd@quoll":{"id":"20260814-resilient-handsome-ibis-d5efdd@quoll","messageId":"20260814-resilient-handsome-ibis-d5efdd@quoll","references":["20260810121121.210040-1-vlad@zlab.su","20260810121121.210040-12-vlad@zlab.su"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260810121121.210040-12-vlad@zlab.su","20260810121121.210040-1-vlad@zlab.su"],"author":{"name":"Krzysztof Kozlowski","address":"krzk@kernel.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Vladislav Leonov","address":"vlad@zlab.su"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"linux-rockchip@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"Simon Glass","address":"sjg@chromium.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-clk@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Conor Dooley","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Heiko Stuebner","address":"heiko@sntech.de"},{"name":"Krzysztof Kozlowski","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Rob Herring","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T10:21:12.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T10:21:12.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 11/25] dt-bindings: i2c: rk3x: Add RV1106 compatible","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Mon, Aug 10, 2026 at 03:11:02PM +0300, Vladislav Leonov wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"The RV1106 I2C controller is compatible with the one found on RK3399,"}],"lineCount":1,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Add RV1106 I2C controller, which is compatible ... /"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"One sentence, one line or two lines."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"so add the \"rockchip,rv1106-i2c\" compatible to the list of variants"},{"depth":1,"text":"that fall back to \"rockchip,rk3399-i2c\"."}],"lineCount":2,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"No need to repeat obvious parts of the diff. Explain non-obvious parts,\nthough, if they are."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Acked-by: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com>"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Best regards,\nKrzysztof"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260810121121.210040-12-vlad@zlab.su"}},"rootIds":["20260814-vivacious-nickel-copperhead-c746f6@quoll","20260814-resilient-handsome-ibis-d5efdd@quoll"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["20260814-vivacious-nickel-copperhead-c746f6@quoll","20260814-resilient-handsome-ibis-d5efdd@quoll"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}